<ArticleLayout title="Form 4547 guide: prepare before you file" description="A step-by-step, non-filing guide to the IRS Trump Account Election form, including who can file, what each election does, and where to submit it." sourceIds={['IRS-TRUMP-ACCOUNTS','IRS-FORM-4547','IRS-FORM-4547-INSTRUCTIONS']}>
  <div class="callout"><strong>Privacy boundary:</strong> this guide does not collect or submit the child’s name, SSN, date of birth, address, or any taxpayer information.</div>
  <h2>What Form 4547 does</h2>
  <p>Form 4547 is used to elect to establish an initial Trump Account and, for an eligible child, to elect the one-time $1,000 Treasury pilot contribution. These are related but separate elections.</p>
  <h2>Step 1: identify the authorized individual</h2>
  <p>For an account-only election, the IRS uses a priority order: legal guardian, parent, adult sibling, then grandparent. A pilot election instead requires the person filing to anticipate that the child will be their qualifying child for the election year.</p>
  <h2>Step 2: confirm the child’s account eligibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Under age 18 at the end of the election year.</li>
    <li>Valid SSN issued before the election.</li>
    <li>No prior initial Trump Account election filed for the child.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Step 3: test the additional pilot requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Birth date from January 1, 2025 through December 31, 2028.</li>
    <li>U.S. citizenship and a valid SSN.</li>
    <li>No prior pilot program contribution election processed.</li>
    <li>Expected qualifying-child relationship for the election year.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a class="button" href="/tools/trump-account-eligibility-checker/">Run the private eligibility check</a></p>
  <h2>Step 4: choose how to submit</h2>
  <p>The IRS currently directs individuals to sign in to an IRS online account and submit Form 4547. The form can also be filed with a current-year e-filed return; paper filing instructions are available in the official instructions. Do not attach Form 4547 to Form 1040-X.</p>
  <h2>Step 5: save confirmation and follow activation instructions</h2>
  <p>Check the submission status through the IRS account and follow Treasury or its agent’s instructions to authenticate and activate the account. An election alone is not the same as a completed, funded account.</p>
